WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.960
WiFI-BC: Learning Efficient Implicit Policies from Demonstrations via Representative Candidate Actions.

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:09.840
Imitation learning algorithms face the dilemma of choosing between task success and inference-time

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:15.040
efficiency. On one side of the scale, we find explicit policies. They are fast during inference

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:19.360
and obtain good results on a range of tasks, but fail to shape proper policies for complex

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:23.920
environments with characteristics like multimodal action distributions. On the other side,

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:29.040
we have implicit and diffusion policies, both able to model complex functions and capture

00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:34.320
multimodality and expert actions. However, they rely on iterative inference processes that increase

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:39.280
latency on every decision. As an alternative, we introduce Wire-Fitting Implicit Behavioral

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:44.000
Cloning, an algorithm that learns a generator that proposes a small set of candidate actions

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:48.640
and a state-action score function. The generator is trained to make a small set of proposals

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:53.440
representative of the score function, pushing one of them to be the maximizer. Therefore,

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:57.840
the inference process consists only of one generation of candidates and a parallel

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:02.160
evaluation for each of them. As a result, we achieve a policy that combines efficient

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:07.120
inference while maintaining high task success. To achieve this, our first component, the

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:11.680
Q-estimator, is trained to score the expert action higher than a set of negative examples.

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:17.200
The training process of the control point generator is inspired by how wire-fitting

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:22.480
interpolation achieves structural maximizability. To make one of the control points the maximizer,

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:26.880
we minimize the error between only the expert action and the closest candidate.

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:31.840
We also maximize their entropy, so they become representative of the complete score function.

00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:36.080
The negative examples generated for training the Q-estimator are a mixture of the top-k

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:41.040
scored candidates and either Langevin samples or noisy expert copies. This negative mining

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:45.280
strategy improves the expressivity of the Q-estimator. Including the top-k control

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:49.840
points allows creating an adversarial synergy between generator and estimator, which pushes

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:54.480
control points to high-scored regions and improves multimodal robustness. To test the

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:58.640
capabilities of WiFI-BC, we tested it against the other baselines in synthetic,

00:01:58.640 --> 00:02:03.680
simulated, and real-world environments. In the simulation environments, we observed that WiFI-BC

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:08.800
obtains task success results on par with implicit behavioral cloning and diffusion policy.

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:14.080
WiFI-BC is always part of the Pareto frontier, except when regression behavioral

00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:18.880
cloning obtains the best task performance. What is more, we demonstrate that WiFI-BC is

00:02:18.880 --> 00:02:23.280
capable of modeling multimodal action distributions. For the real-world environment,

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:28.720
we train the algorithms on the Push-T task. We observe that WiFI-BC achieves the best results

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:32.880
in terms of intersection over union and is the second-fastest method after regression

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:37.600
behavioral cloning. In summary, we propose an implicit behavioral cloning algorithm that

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:42.400
combines a control point generator and a Q-estimator to balance policy success and inference

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:47.600
time efficiency. Through our experiments, we demonstrate that WiFI-BC achieves the best

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:51.440
trade-off across comparison behavioral cloning methods. Thank you.
